  "rust_summary": "an entity's state flags through an `EntityRef`: sneaking, sprinting, water and lava, fire, air, silence, invisibility and pose.",
  "doc_summary": "`entity.is_shift_key_down(host)`, `is_crouching`, `is_sprinting`, `is_in_water`, `is_in_lava`, `fire_immune`, `fire_ticks`, `air_supply`, `max_air_supply`, `is_silent`, `set_silent(host, silent)`, `is_invisible` and `pose` (`standing`, `crouching`...). Players and mobs have them all; other kinds return `None` for what Horizon doesn't keep for them. Bundles need \"hooks\": @API:entity_state@.",
